// spec: a backslash at the end of a line inside a string literal splices the next line on, as C++'s translation phase 2 does: the backslash and the newline are not in the string (the next line's leading spaces are); a constant's literal the same
// factorio: the unit tests' multi-line Lua commands (TestLuaSurface's EmptyMapGenSettingsReadWriteStability, ChunkBounds, DestroyRoboportWithTriggerWhenSpawningRobotsForLogistics): the command text a test echoes to the console kept a newline per splice, so the map's console and its CRC differed from the C++ build's
// pending: a spliced literal keeps the newline (codegen's and consteval's escape decoding take `\` + newline as a newline)
constexpr const char* constant = "ab\
cd";
int main()
{
  const char* text = "local a = 1;\
   local b = 2";
  println("[{}] {} [{}] {}", text, strlen(text), constant, strlen(constant));
  return 0;
}
